        "text_sha256": "db40417adb1e52554814c3939af43096ce4c661b79173992be35aca343231171",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000064",
        "block_index": 64,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Lobster",
        "text_sha256": "3bc406963f13878049e7881dd132cbd8b2b4f578a5670ea38c5630fe2f064a21",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000065",
        "block_index": 65,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Hake",
        "text_sha256": "774a12adbf31c0c6b417287463d1a9a56e6cc03747af774417b5ecedad44cbd4",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000066",
        "block_index": 66,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Clams",
        "text_sha256": "32ac313e72a8068dce21c163f020affc94bd970835bc708440d3494289623739",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000067",
        "block_index": 67,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Black sea bass",
        "text_sha256": "24241d02cbc69a9490c0d8416932b9f27f2ac3cf783ee122eb05e3f3ec67893a",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000068",
        "block_index": 68,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Anchovies",
        "text_sha256": "79d7596d7afaff436fdc62e38259776e83a6af72a3f3139125375a478d36049c",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000069",
        "block_index": 69,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Trout",
        "text_sha256": "7e200362473bfd0879ccdec4163b86cbef339f29ef4cc1f8e8b2d90226595454",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000070",
        "block_index": 70,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Heard conflicting advice on salmon during pregnancy? Salmon is definitely one of nature's best providers of DHA. But to avoid the higher levels of PCBs often found in farmed salmon, opt for wild (which also contains more of those healthy omega-3 fats) or organic farmed salmon.",
        "text_sha256": "9a6886a7c8a6476bc3865452624a26789f8f08e22be59fbe2408ffff41d86301",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000071",
        "block_index": 71,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How to properly prepare fish during pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "9045800957f416a20d0bb64a372244fd09aeb56f5105da54c9627e3020504389",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000072",
        "block_index": 72,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "By now you’ve probably heard that you should avoid sushi during pregnancy — and the same goes for any other raw (oysters, ceviche, smoked salmon) or undercooked fish, since they can contain bacteria and parasites (like Listeria ) that are dangerous for your developing baby.",
        "text_sha256": "f57f3e4b484fc4e1220a631202c14f5ffb54d9e019d8757fb5df0295b89cee6a",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000073",
        "block_index": 73,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here are a few tips on how to prepare fish that will reduce your exposure to any potential contaminants:",
        "text_sha256": "3cc9e18100706213b1edb8d8598588133853daf62838c4d99837b66a39b907ee",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000074",
        "block_index": 74,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "If you're buying fresh seafood, properly refrigerate it. Store it in the fridge in a sealed container if you’re not cooking it immediately.",
        "text_sha256": "70685d60586ce2d20b903bb1addf304c88bc9bf6d4f3cbc543128a90bcd7fa41",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000075",
        "block_index": 75,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Use separate cutting boards for meats (including fish) and fruits/veggies.",
        "text_sha256": "7075d49f8f8442c88d02e07452d8c05c34fa49a4410b6bd706d4dbddc48b269f",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000076",
        "block_index": 76,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Don't reuse marinades.",
        "text_sha256": "bf6755124f62ba2ab9d4907796207851a56ecb88a91c0a0a83596756ad61efae",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000077",
        "block_index": 77,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cook seafood (all types, including shucked clams, oysters, shrimp, lobster, and scallops) until it reaches an internal temperature of 145° Fahrenheit. If a thermometer isn’t available, you’ll know it’s done when the flesh is opaque (milky white) and the filets flake easily with a fork.",
        "text_sha256": "df31a431a887a7ccf826683925de1cabd441e45dac7fb5857853c3869d2b54ad",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000078",
        "block_index": 78,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cook clams, mussels, and oysters still in their shells until they open; throw away any that don’t.",
        "text_sha256": "4f0dc51b0314934ec2ea30c9141b1b38ff6860476a383e233d1230b9d0c7a23f",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000079",
        "block_index": 79,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Benefits of fish during pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "e0a78702341fb8d28dcb3bce41c7d2a5589c467b327a642fe590af9ec37539b0",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000080",
        "block_index": 80,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The good news (at least for moms who enjoy seafood) is that fish really does offer big benefits for both pregnant women and their developing babies. Eating fish:",
        "text_sha256": "840adcaea60e44b531d66c66c90c5f815c17225c8b94beab384bda6901ba14ac",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000081",
        "block_index": 81,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Supports fetal growth. Fish is a first-rate source of lean protein and its essential amino acids that help create all of your baby’s cells — from skin and muscle to hair and bones.",
        "text_sha256": "eff34d469e1181d2fde6ebad27c28b67a6fe084a86b7b4b108b850c8a63de859",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000082",
        "block_index": 82,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Is good for your baby’s brain. Fattier varieties of fish in particular, like salmon, are a source of the omega-3 fatty acid DHA, which has been shown to boost baby brain power. It’s more important than ever in the third trimester, when your baby’s brain growth is fast and furious.",
        "text_sha256": "4e9092244293ae24bf6742d9ce76dea88dad0061907ce6bdca7395ecea02fd60",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000083",
        "block_index": 83,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Boosts your memory. Speaking of boosted brain power, getting enough omega-3s may also improve your memory — especially helpful when you’re battling a case of pregnancy brain .",
        "text_sha256": "222c3dd00da3498670897b24298d6f34c2d877cb75f0dc31c2f25f316daebcfe",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000084",
        "block_index": 84,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Improves your mood. An adequate intake of omega-3 fatty acids and especially DHA may decrease your risk of depression during pregnancy as well as postpartum depression.",
        "text_sha256": "344f5e92ab28469c146006a35b9b2e40e8b3cc5a597ad30747c6cff4538e5884",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000085",
        "block_index": 85,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Supports your heart. A diet rich in fish can lower your risk of cardiac disease by reducing blood clotting and levels of triglycerides (blood fat) as well as lowering blood pressure if you have preexisting hypertension.",
        "text_sha256": "80ca35729b3be7219990047c0b72156e83ce5a4c3673412a655520150f279a12",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000086",
        "block_index": 86,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "May reduce risk of preterm birth. Scientists have observed that rates of preterm birth are lower in areas where people eat a lot of fish — and some studies have indeed linked adequate omega 3 intake (whether through fish or supplements) to a lower risk of preterm birth.",
        "text_sha256": "c5cd600ca4ea116655ebd123c2ef146e1a94f4e2c133b67a9a5a600aeb162b6c",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000087",
        "block_index": 87,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Want more daily tips on what's safe, as well as expert-backed advice? Give the What to Expect app a try — it's like having a pregnancy buddy in your pocket.",
        "text_sha256": "b36b4892c5c2a68e67e97326e1a6138cc67c2da17b1afe9ff46eca839a83bbaf",
        "word_count": 30
      }
    ],
